<InfoPage title="From first dial to the next step." description="Outbound reaches out. Inbound picks up. Your team keeps the customer context.">
 <h2 id="outbound">Outbound: work the leads you want to reach.</h2><p>Your rep chooses a contact or calling queue. Multi-line dialing can try several leads while the rep is available, select a live answer, and manage the other attempts. Local presence can select an available number for the area being called.</p><p>Starter includes one line. Professional, Agency and Enterprise include 3, 10 and 30 calling lines and numbers. Active numbers and caller ID selection determine the effective line count; choosing one fixed caller ID uses one line.</p>
 <h2 id="inbound">Inbound: connect the customer who called you.</h2><p>A customer calls your routing number. The queue looks for an eligible rep, offers the call, and connects the two sides after acceptance. An answered offer and a completed connection are different states; the routing system tracks both.</p><p>Set team availability, waiting limits and callback or voicemail fallbacks during onboarding.</p>
 <h2 id="routing">Calling decisions your team can understand.</h2><p>Outbound selection considers the calling strategy and its available evidence. Inbound checks queue rules, rep eligibility, and capacity before offering a call. The goal is to use the next available opportunity well, while keeping the decision and its outcome traceable.</p>
 <h2 id="analytics">Keep the history behind the follow-up.</h2><p>Review calls, outcomes and customer context to decide what to do next. A missed call, a completed conversation and an unconfirmed connection need different follow-up.</p>
 <h2 id="transcripts">Review the conversation when transcription is enabled.</h2><p>Agency and Enterprise include recordings and transcription. Workspace settings and permissions determine whether they are used for a call. Add Mercury coaching for script guidance, suggested responses and transcript review.</p>
 <a class="setup-action" href="/get-started">PLAN YOUR SETUP →</a>
</InfoPage>
